      "Then He Kissed Me and Poor Side of Town (the opened and closed hat he is credited with popularising) have tabs, but each began as an AI transcription: transcribe them from the records.",
      "Read his memoir, Hal Blaine and the Wrecking Crew (with David Goggin, 1990), and the NAMM oral history.",
      "His kits by year: only the blue sparkle Ludwig and the fibreglass concert toms of the Monster set are seen; sizes and the year the Monster set came in are not in what was read.",
      "Whether the drummer in the 1966 Good Vibrations studio film is Blaine: identified from the session, not from a caption."
