    "roles": ["session", "band_member"],
    "summary": "The session drummer of 1960s Los Angeles and, by his own count, on 35,000 recordings: the Wrecking Crew, which he named, behind Phil Spector's Wall of Sound, Brian Wilson's Beach Boys, the Byrds, the Mamas & the Papas, Simon & Garfunkel, Sinatra and Elvis. A big-band reader taught by Krupa's teacher Roy Knapp, he liked rock and roll and played for the record: Be My Baby's snare on 4 alone, the snare doubled on the floor tom, the snare on every beat to lift a chorus, a cannon shot by an elevator shaft. Six Grammy Records of the Year in a row; 'May he rest forever on 2 and 4'."
  },
